api_examples:
Request schema example:
{
  "query": "How to rotate logs",
  "candidates": [
    {"id": "doc:123", "text": "Rotate logs with logrotate...", "metadata": {"source": "kb"}},
    {"id": "doc:456", "text": "Use systemd timers...", "metadata": {"source": "forum"}}
  ],
  "top_k": 3,
  "score_cutoff": 0.12,
  "pagination": {"cursor": null, "page_size": 100}
}
Response schema example:
{
  "results": [
    {"id": "doc:123", "rank": 1, "score": 0.77, "norm_score": 0.98, "payload": {"snippet": "Rotate logs with logrotate..."}, "provenance": {"embedding_model": "ada-emb-2"}},
    {"id": "doc:456", "rank": 2, "score": 0.43, "norm_score": 0.55, "payload": {"snippet": "Use systemd timers..."}}
  ],
  "top_k_requested": 3,
  "cursor": "eyJvZmZzZXQiOjEwMH0="
}
Notes: cursor is opaque base64 JSON, clients SHOULD not rely on structure. Structured output splits "payload" (user content) from "provenance" and "scores" for easy downstream storage and auditing.
